==County coding==
Montana established a numeric county-code system for its license plates in 1934, which remains in use today (except on optional plates). With some exceptions, the order of the codes is based on the respective populations of the state's 56 counties according to the [[1930 United States census]].<ref>{{cite news |title=What's the deal with Montana's license plate numbering system? |url=https://billingsgazette.com/news/state-and-regional/montana/whats-the-deal-with-montanas-license-plate-numbering-system/article_119837d9-3863-5951-a163-066c86fd86af.html |newspaper=[[Billings Gazette]] |date=May 2, 2014 |access-date=January 2, 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Montana County Seats & Corresponding License Plate Numbers |url=https://www.mtcounties.org/counties/county-seats-corresponding-license-plate-numbers/ |publisher=Montana Association of Counties |access-date=January 2, 2022}}</ref>
